BIT-15: Average each link's segments once for all species

Saving a reporting period averaged each link's segments once per species
and wrote every value with its own fwrite; MSXgetqual() walked a link's
segments once per species too. Average all species of a link in one walk
(in parallel when saving), write each period with one fwrite, and let
MSXgetqual() compute a link's species once per step. This assumes
concentrations change only in MSXinit and MSXstep, as every toolkit
function does today.

Requires: none
Results: identical (every concentration, the output file and the report are unchanged)

Apply from the root of an EPANET-MSX checkout at 85a303d, after FIX-01, FIX-02 and BIT-01 to BIT-14:
    git apply --whitespace=nowarn BIT-15.patch
or use tools/build-msx.sh, which applies the series in order.

